# What is tracked here is the source of the two videos: the plans, the scenes,
# the narration pipeline, the render scripts and the recording booth. Everything
# a render or a recording session produces is left out — it is reproducible from
# that source, and it is hundreds of megabytes.

# The Manim checkout both cuts install from — one copy at the root, which each
# version's venv installs from with `pip install -e ../manim`. Upstream and
# unmodified, so it is cloned per machine rather than vendored here:
#   git clone https://github.com/ManimCommunity/manim.git
#   git -C manim checkout v0.22.0
/manim/

# Virtualenvs — rebuilt per machine, see each version's README.
.venv/

# Manim's own output. Two things in here are tracked, so that someone who has
# only cloned the repo can still see the animation while they record: the
# 1080p60 scene renders the booth plays, and the beat-timing logs that say
# where each line sits in them. They are a matched pair — the logs carry the
# frame rate they were measured at, and a beat lands in a different place at
# 15fps than at 60fps — so both come from the same render. `./render.sh -qh`
# writes both together, which is the one you already run for the final cut.
# Everything else here is a cache.
#
# Git cannot re-include a path inside an excluded directory, so each level is
# opened in turn rather than excluding media/ outright.
**/media/*
!**/media/timing/
!**/media/videos/
**/media/videos/*
!**/media/videos/scenes/
**/media/videos/scenes/*
!**/media/videos/scenes/1080p60/
# ...but not the per-animation fragments Manim stitches each scene from.
**/media/videos/scenes/1080p60/partial_movie_files/

# The stitched cuts and the per-scene mixes behind them.
renders/

# Narration is tracked, not ignored: whoever records a line pushes it, and
# whoever renders pulls it. So `audio/*.mp3` and friends stay in the repo, and
# so does `audio/.scratch.json` — it is the list of lines that are still a
# machine `say` placeholder rather than a real read, and `narrate.py scratch
# --refresh` speaks over anything on it. It has to arrive with the recordings
# or a real take can be overwritten as if it were a placeholder.
#
# What is left out is only what each machine makes for itself:

# The raw per-take history behind the booth's undo key, and its index. Local to
# whoever did the recording — a render only ever reads audio/<line>.mp3 — and it
# grows with every retake.
**/audio/takes/
**/audio/.takes.json

# Measurement cache, keyed on each file's mtime and size. Git does not preserve
# mtime, so every entry would be a miss on arrival anyway; it is rebuilt on the
# first retime or mix.
**/audio/.measured.json

# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]

# macOS
.DS_Store
